  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: an error composing the service-request set denies (empty set), never throws into a permissive path. Scope: the new compose branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02">No regression in request cost — the ISS-003 fix MUST NOT add unconditional per-request Dataverse round trips beyond the existing composition budget. ⚠️ This constraint is under real pressure here: the service-request check is inherently a READ ("is sprk_requestedby me?"), unlike the other three roots which answer from an already-composed set. Make it conditional (only on the service-request-parented path), not unconditional, and state the measured round-trip count in the PR. Scope: the ISS-003 resolution path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">BFF-touching: placement decision cited from .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md in the PR; publish size measured and reported (ceiling 60 MB). Scope: PR description.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Root sets remain roots-only — do NOT add child-entity accessible sets (AccessibleCommunicationIds etc.); FR-26 stamps make them unnecessary and 06 §F1 shows they would be 2-hop. Scope: whole task; adding a child-entity set is an escalation, not a decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-09 (task 028)">🔴 BINDING, DO NOT RE-LITIGATE. "Service requests are internally submitted records; they are sent via the SPA by internal workforce users; the service request is not accessible by external users (e.g., law firms)." Scope: the whole task. Therefore `CallerPrincipal` composes exactly THREE externally-grantable root sets and MUST NOT gain a fourth; `GrantSupportedRootEntities` MUST NOT gain `sprk_servicerequest`; no service-request lookup may be added to `sprk_externalrecordaccess`. ⚠️ Do NOT overcorrect into "a service request is not core" — that is a different false claim. It IS core (nothing else confers access to it); it is simply never externally grantable, and the grant table's deliberate omission is the evidence for the distinction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests at KEEP paths (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests + seam tests where the suite already covers root composition); no Mock of HttpMessageHandler. Scope: new tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

