  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">🔴 GATE — DO NOT SKIP. Confirm the owner has answered ISS-003's product question (what may a requester DO to their own service request's to-dos). If it is still unanswered, STOP and escalate per the trigger below; this task cannot be correctly scoped without it. Then read the AS-MERGED Phase 1/2 shapes and notes/task-028-service-request-root.md before editing anything.</step>
    <step order="1">Re-scope this POML's goal, steps and acceptance criteria to the owner's answer, and record the re-scope in notes/ before writing code. The three negatives in the acceptance criteria are NOT re-scopable — they hold whatever the answer is.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the ISS-003 fix by the owner-selected mechanism, honoring the rights-shape constraint: the service-request check is a Dataverse read ("is sprk_requestedby me?"), not a set-membership test. If it needs to sit behind a signature that is pure everywhere else, surface that design choice rather than silently making `RightsForRoot` impure.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify the existing service-requests module (sprk_requestedby dimension, plane-gated) still behaves identically — do NOT change its descriptor here, and do NOT duplicate its scoping logic.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: the ISS-003 case (a workforce submitter reaches a to-do parented to their own service request, at the level the owner specified) PLUS the three standing negatives — no AccessibleServiceRequestIds set, GrantSupportedRootEntities still exactly three, a CIAM partner still gets an empty service-request set server-side.</step>
    <step order="5">dotnet build + test green; publish size + round-trip count reported.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md; note decisions in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner has not answered ISS-003's product question (what may a requester DO to their own service request's to-dos — read? write? create?), STOP at step 0. Inventing a verb set to close the task is exactly how the level asymmetry got into task 009.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any proposed implementation would add a service-request lookup to `sprk_externalrecordaccess`, add an accessible-service-request set to `CallerPrincipal`, or extend `GrantSupportedRootEntities`, STOP — all three are forbidden by the owner's 2026-09-09 ruling and none may be re-litigated at implementation time. An always-empty set that looks like a fix is worse than the gap: the next reader "completes" the model by adding the missing grant lookup.</trigger>
    <trigger>If closing ISS-003 cannot be done without making `RightsForRoot` (or its as-merged successor) perform I/O where it is pure for the other three roots, STOP and escalate the design rather than changing that signature's contract silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

