  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The ISS-003 over-denial is closed at the level the owner specified: a workforce user who submitted service request SR1 is no longer denied on a to-do parented to SR1. (The exact verb set is fixed by the owner's ISS-003 answer and MUST be transcribed into this criterion during step 1, not invented at implementation time.)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative — THE LOAD-BEARING ONE: no `AccessibleServiceRequestIds` (or equivalently-named) set exists on CallerPrincipal after this task; grep is clean. A service request is core but NEVER externally grantable (owner ruling 2026-09-09, task 028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `GrantSupportedRootEntities` still contains EXACTLY { sprk_project, sprk_matter, sprk_workassignment } — the grant allow-list was NOT extended to sprk_servicerequest, and no lookup was added to sprk_externalrecordaccess.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a CIAM partner caller still resolves an EMPTY service-request set server-side (the existing module's plane gate), so internal-only never depends on the client hiding a tab.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no AccessibleCommunicationIds / AccessibleEventIds / AccessibleInvoiceIds set exists anywhere after this task (grep clean) — child sets stay banned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Regression: existing project/matter/workassignment composition tests pass unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; publish size ≤ 60 MB reported; per-request Dataverse round-trip count stated and within NFR-02.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-27; 06 §F1.

AMENDED 2026-09-15 (register triage); the amendment was PROMOTED OUT OF THIS NOTES BLOCK into every binding element by task 115 on 2026-09-21. Until then the title, prompt, goal, steps and acceptance criteria all still asserted the retired premise, so an executor reading the file top-down would have built the refused thing and only met the correction at the bottom. That is the defect class task 115 exists to remove — a note cannot bind when the binding elements contradict it.

- RETIRED: a service-request set filled from sprk_externalrecordaccess grants, with the grant allow-list extended to sprk_servicerequest. It contradicts the owner's 2026-09-09 ruling (task 028): service requests are NEVER externally grantable, and CallerPrincipal must not carry an accessible-service-request set (project CLAUDE.md; notes/task-028-service-request-root.md §5).
- REMAINING IN-SCOPE WORK: ISS-003 (#964) — the workforce user who submitted a service request is denied PATCH /api/v1/external/todos/{id} on to-dos parented to it.
- STILL BLOCKED ON THE OWNER: (1) the ISS-003 product question — what may a requester DO to their own service request's to-dos; (2) re-scope this POML's goal, steps and criteria to that answer.
- Tasks 055 and 056 were written to consume the retired fourth root set; both were repaired by task 115 at the same time. Re-read them as repaired, not as remembered.</notes>

